      "title": "U.S. International Transactions and Investment Position, 2nd Quarter 2026",
      "summary": "<p>The U.S. current-account deficit resulting from international economic transactions widened by $33.4 billion, or 15.7 percent, to $246.0 billion in the second quarter of 2026, according to statistics released today by the U.S. Bureau of Economic Analysis. The revised first-quarter deficit was $212.6 billion. The second-quarter deficit was 3.0 percent of current-dollar gross domestic product, up from 2.7 percent in the first quarter.</p>\n      <p>The U.S. net international investment position, the difference between U.S. residents' foreign financial assets and liabilities, was &ndash;$22.42 trillion at the end of the second quarter of 2026. Assets totaled $46.97 trillion, and liabilities totaled $69.39 trillion. At the end of the first quarter of 2026, the net investment position was &ndash;$21.27 trillion (revised).</p>",
